  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A circle has a radius of \\(\\log_{10}(a^2)\\) and a circumference of \\(\\log_{10}(b^4).\\) What is \\(\\log_a b?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4\\pi}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{\\pi}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\pi\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2\\pi\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(10^{2\\pi}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2008-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The circumference is \\(2\\pi\\) times the radius, so \\[ \\log_{10}(b^4) = 2\\pi \\log_{10}(a^2). \\]\n\nRewriting, \\(4\\log_{10} b = 4\\pi \\log_{10} a,\\) hence \\(\\log_{10} b = \\pi \\log_{10} a.\\)\n\nTherefore \\(\\log_a b = \\dfrac{\\log_{10} b}{\\log_{10} a} = \\pi.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Circumference equals \\(2\\pi\\) times the radius",
        "Use \\(\\log_{10}(a^2) = 2\\log_{10} a\\) and \\(\\log_{10}(b^4) = 4\\log_{10} b,\\) then form \\(\\dfrac{\\log_{10} b}{\\log_{10} a}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
